  "about": "Counting on through the hundreds to 150: what comes next after 109, 119 and 129, what comes just before, and recognising a number like 132 when he hears it. NC.1.NBT.1 asks him to count aloud to 150 from any number; NC only requires reading and writing numerals to 100 (NC.1.NBT.7), so the three-digit numerals here support the oral count rather than test writing them.",
